From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 20:19:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: let agents manage chat link rules and tell them the
 active syntaxes

Agents set up most of a user's tooling, so they should be able to add a
link rule when asked ("link BST-123 to our Jira"), and they should write
references in the form the chat links instead of wrapping them in code.

- sys_link_rules lists, adds, updates and removes rules, git hosts included.
  The runner proxies it to /v1/link-rules: it applies one change to the rules
  it read, checks the list with the server's validator and saves it with
  that version, so a concurrent edit from Settings is refused rather than
  overwritten. It is a framework tool group (tool_groups.link_rules) and
  rides the native relay.
- Rules run in every viewer's browser, so every add, update and remove asks
  the user first: __ask_on_link_rule_change joins the approval policies
  every engine carries, and the tool skips the no-policy fast path, like the
  scheduled-task tools. Listing is not gated.
- A framework instruction names each enabled rule's syntax (session:<id>,
  ABC-123 for a short form) so agents write them as plain text. When the
  workspace is a git checkout (a stat walk for .git), a second sentence asks
  for issue #123 or PR #123 rather than a bare #123, and owner/repo#123 for
  another repository, naming the provider's !123 only when the workspace
  remote's git rule uses it; outside a checkout it is left out. SDK harnesses
  get it per turn from rules and a workspace remote the runner rereads after
  a minute; native Claude and Codex get it at launch, from the runner or from
  omnigent claude/codex, so a rule changed mid-session reaches their prompt
  on the next launch. A failed read just leaves it out.

Not upstream yet: proposed from feat/chat-link-rules, the git-reference part from
feat/git-ref-notation; drop this copy once they merge.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
